---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import products from '../../data/products.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The 5-Minute Rule for Productivity | NoMore5Mins"
  description="How committing to just five minutes can help you overcome procrastination, build momentum, and tackle even the most daunting tasks on your list."
  type="article"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <article>
      <header class="mb-10">
        <a href="/blog/" class="text-sm text-amber-500 hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors">&larr; Back to Blog</a>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-slate-50 sm:text-5xl">
          The 5-Minute Rule for Productivity
        </h1>
        <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-slate-400 dark-muted">
          <span>By NoMore5Mins Team</span>
          <span class="text-slate-600">|</span>
          <time datetime="2026-04">April 2026</time>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400 dark-muted">
        <p>
          Procrastination often comes from feeling overwhelmed by the size of a task. The
          5-Minute Rule flips that on its head: commit to working on something for just five
          minutes. If you want to stop after five minutes, you can. But most of the time, you
          will not want to. Starting is the hardest part, and five minutes is all it takes to
          build momentum. This upcoming guide explores the psychology behind the rule and how
          to put it into practice.
        </p>

        <div class="card text-center">
          <p class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-amber-500">Coming Soon</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-400 dark-muted">
            This article is currently being written. Check back soon for the full guide.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/timer/"
            class="mt-4 inline-block text-amber-500 hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors font-medium"
          >
            Try the NoMore5Mins Timer &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4">
    <ProductGrid
      title="Productivity Boosters"
      subtitle="Tools to help you make every 5 minutes count"
      products={products.productivity.slice(0, 2)}
      columns={2}
    />
  </div>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
